# .NET build output — must never enter the build context. If these leak in,
# `COPY src/ src/` in src/PedeLocal.Api/Dockerfile overwrites the container's
# own `dotnet restore` output with the host's obj/project.assets.json, which
# hardcodes the host's absolute NuGet packageFolders path (e.g.
# C:\Users\<user>\.nuget\packages). That path doesn't exist in the Linux
# build stage, so `dotnet publish --no-restore` fails with NETSDK1064
# ("package ... was not found") even though restore succeeded moments
# earlier inside the container.
**/bin/
**/obj/

# VCS / IDE / OS
.git/
.gitignore
.vs/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Test results / coverage
**/[Tt]est[Rr]esult*/
*.trx
*.coverage
*.coveragexml

# Publish output
publish/
*.pubxml

# Env / secrets — never bake these into an image
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Logs
logs/
*.log

# Docs / misc not needed for build
docs/
*.md
